pe":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/json","state":"uploaded","size":652,"digest":"sha256:aa71e9c3e84275afd943bd54a296d4a0414654c6e9aec03e50c818a06d318c02","download_count":0,"created_at":"2026-11-16T20:40:20Z","updated_at":"2026-11-16T20:40:20Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/releases/download/m126-v0.12.6/m12stage6-starter-manifest.json"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enginsoysal/engacer-os/tarball/m126-v0.12.6","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enginsoysal/engacer-os/zipball/m126-v0.12.6","body":"# Engacer OS M12.6 / 0.12.6 — Files presentation\n\nNative qualification passes **M12-STAGE6-VM-v1**.\n[Exact-source acceptance](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/f7eb0df6b9dc0fdcab6af9eae6700374af2ba97f/evidence/M12/6/acceptance-results.json) verifies\n581 compiled Git inputs, ten native journeys, separate actual 150%/4K name-tip\nprofiles, twelve cached/full comparisons and matching VMware/BIOS install and\nordinary starts. Public release and full website proof close separately before M12.7.\n\nBuild: `a4efdd3ede571e885ec1780fbcc0d3f7`.\nISO SHA256: `5c72697dacdf12e2eb7c2d483729620f36ab2f0d51dc04498a9a0342b15d3a19`.\nVMware ZIP SHA256: `44c9221b03bea49c41bcbf6b1676c4e057703f58bdc39b4801ccc447c2de2ff7`.\n\n## What changes\n\nDetails prioritizes readable names, adapts Type/Size columns to the available\nwidth and offers real native sort headings with direction indicators. Natural\nname ordering places File2 before File10. Type sorting uses the displayed type\nnames, and folders stay first in either direction. Stable source IDs preserve\nselection and keyboard anchors. Switching views reveals a focused selected item.\n\nIcons uses original 48-pixel artwork with centered two-line, ellipsized names.\nA measured name tip reveals the complete supported filename. Its drawing checks\nthe actual topmost window and row; a stale hover target must not leave a tip\nover another window. Active/inactive selection, hover and keyboard focus differ.\nBreadcrumbs retain intermediate folders when they fit and explicitly mark an\nomitted middle. Edit continues to expose the full supported address.\n\nNative and USB share presentation geometry, real names, extension-based type\nlabels and actual file sizes. These labels do not validate file contents, and no\ntimestamps or recursive folder sizes are invented. USB retains its directory\norder and existing FAT32, six-visible-entry, one-file create-only capabilities;\nUSB sorting stays unavailable. Icon-grid keys and page controls follow that bound.\nNative view/order preferences reuse the existing 32 records. The separate USB\nview preference is a validated 16-byte per-user record, independent of device\nidentity and optional for normal startup.\n\n[Architecture and choices](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/f7eb0df6b9dc0fdcab6af9eae6700374af2ba97f/docs/architecture/files-m126.md),\n[Files views guide](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/f7eb0df6b9dc0fdcab6af9eae6700374af2ba97f/docs/handbook/files-m126.md),\n[eight-step installation](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/f7eb0df6b9dc0fdcab6af9eae6700374af2ba97f/docs/handbook/install-m126.md).\n\n## Qualification boundary\n\nNative qualification must cover real installation, actual differently sized\nfiles, sorting/reverse/selection, complete-name tips and occlusion, both views,\nminimum size, real USB metadata/keys/detach, saved preferences across ordinary\nboots and actual 150%/4K. Its matching VMware ZIP, separate BIOS installation and\nindependent starts, twelve cached/full comparisons and idle/resource checks\nremain required. Host comparator and geometry tests supplement native evidence.\n\nThe first candidate's probe found a stale name tip after keyboard window/location\nchanges. That candidate is not accepted; its report remains in diagnostics.\nTwo test-observer assumptions were also corrected: an off-screen caption needs\na reachable keyboard close route, and Files' actual minimum height is 420 pixels.\nThey are not reported as kernel or installer failures.\n\nFile commands/dialogs continue in their ordered next stages. Shared-menu footer\nfitting and HiDPI cursor-versus-hit isolation remain M12.14/M12.16 follow-ups.\nThe earlier concurrent BIOS/AHCI observation remains open for M12.18; stress\nreliability is unqualified. Final comprehensive controller/application regression\nis M12.18. Physical hardware, ARM, vendor GPU 3D and universal DOS/Windows\ncompatibility are outside this stage. Agent review is not a human usability study.\n\nFixed shell state is **545,636 bytes**, **16 bytes** above M12.5 and\n**1,808 bytes** above M11.6. Tasks retain zero managed pages/new allocation\nfailures; idle CPUs halt. Main managed memory returns to 4,288,512 bytes, with\na 4,337,664-byte measured peak. Font coverage is unchanged at 251,248 bytes;\nraster icon cache is zero and the temporary icon row is 512 bytes.\n[Resources](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/f7eb0df6b9dc0fdcab6af9eae6700374af2ba97f/evidence/M12/6/resources.json) separate fixed state, managed\ndisplay/device pages and configured RAM. Observer event/drain timings are not FPS.\n\n![Actual installed Files icon view](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/f7eb0df6b9dc0fdcab6af9eae6700374af2ba97f/evidence/M12/6/feature.png)\n"}